# Data Management System

## Overview

AiTrainer manages various types of data including user profiles, workout records, exercise definitions, and pose detection results. The data management system handles storage, retrieval, and synchronization of this information.

## Key Components

### Data Entities
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/entity/UserEntity.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/entity/UserEntity.kt): User profile information
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/entity/PoseEntity.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/entity/PoseEntity.kt): Exercise pose definitions and metadata

### Storage
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/sql/](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/sql): Local database for persistent data storage
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/utils/FileUtils.kt](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/utils/FileUtils.kt): File system utilities for storing pose data and images

### Data Processing
- [app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/datacenter/](mdc:app/src/main/java/com/lindum/mlkit/vision/datacenter): Data processing and synchronization logic

## Data Workflow

1. User profile data is stored in UserEntity and persisted to local storage
2. Exercise pose definitions are loaded from assets and stored in PoseEntity objects
3. During workouts, pose detection results are processed and analyzed
4. Workout results are saved to the local database
5. Historical workout data is available for review in the Diary section
